WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.494
Shampoo, Conditioning Shampoo and Hair Conditioner. This is module 3 of the course.

2
00:00:06.817 --> 00:00:11.717
Hair products sell on feel, so today we make all three and test them on real hair.

3
00:00:12.717 --> 00:00:18.448
Afro-textured hair tends to be dry, because scalp oil doesn't travel easily along the coils.

4
00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:23.300
So the shampoo in these bottles should clean the scalp well but stop short of squeaky.

5
00:00:23.686 --> 00:00:32.905
Compared with the hand wash, we raise CAPB from 5% to 7% and add panthenol, provitamin B5, to help hair hold water.

6
00:00:33.905 --> 00:00:38.855
Ifeoma in Owerri checked her assistant's sheet before her first 12 kg batch.

7
00:00:39.224 --> 00:00:47.556
The non-water lines came to 3,084 g, so water had to be 8,916 g. It matched.

8
00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:54.672
Notice the panthenol going onto the small scale. Tiny amounts need the precise scale, not the platform one.

9
00:00:55.672 --> 00:01:00.454
In the bucket, dissolve EDTA in the water, keeping about 10% back for brine.

10
00:01:00.866 --> 00:01:06.116
Dissolve the SLES slowly with gentle stirring, then add CAPB, glycerin and panthenol.

11
00:01:06.574 --> 00:01:10.360
Premix the fragrance with a little CAPB and add it with the preservative.

12
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:19.489
Now the strip. Shampoo should be slightly acidic, about 5 to 6. Adjust with the 1% sample method from module 1.

13
00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:28.060
Thicken with salt brine after a step test, a little thicker than your hand wash. Then rest it overnight and check it before filling.

14
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:37.934
Most shampoos sting the eyes. Your label must say: avoid contact with eyes, and if contact occurs, rinse well with clean water, like this.

15
00:01:38.303 --> 00:01:44.084
Don't write tear-free, anti-dandruff or hair growth unless you have the testing and NAFDAC approval.

16
00:01:45.084 --> 00:01:51.014
For a 2-in-1, a small amount of cationic polymer leaves a thin film on hair when you rinse.

17
00:01:51.406 --> 00:01:59.850
The powder lumps if you tip it in. So Kemi stirred her 30 g of guar into the glycerin first, then poured the slurry into stirring water.

18
00:02:00.288 --> 00:02:05.568
After 30 minutes, smooth and slightly thick, she carried on with the normal shampoo method.

19
00:02:06.568 --> 00:02:13.040
Prove it works. Wash two identical hair bundles, one with each bottle, then count comb strokes while wet.

20
00:02:13.404 --> 00:02:20.407
Never make a 2-in-1 by pouring a conditioner or quat disinfectant into shampoo. It goes cloudy and separates.

21
00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:28.702
Now the conditioner, a cream that doesn't foam. Weigh phase A into a steel pot, and write down the empty pot weight first.

22
00:02:29.103 --> 00:02:36.256
Phase B, the waxes, goes in a second pot. BTMS-50 pastilles both emulsify and condition.

23
00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:42.111
Melted wax at 75 degrees causes serious burns and sticks to skin.

24
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:49.238
Wear long sleeves, closed shoes and heat-resistant gloves. Turn pot handles inwards and keep children out.

25
00:02:50.238 --> 00:02:57.264
Both pots heat in water baths to about 75 degrees. Hold them 10 to 15 minutes so all the wax melts.

26
00:02:57.674 --> 00:03:03.469
Watch: phase B pours into phase A, with short bursts of a stick blender for 2 to 3 minutes.

27
00:03:03.807 --> 00:03:09.320
Keep stirring as it cools. See it turn thick and creamy between about 50 and 40 degrees.

28
00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:15.654
Only below 40 degrees do the preservative and fragrance go in. They are heat-sensitive.

29
00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:26.014
If hot wax touches skin, cool the burn under cool running water for at least 20 minutes, and seek medical care for anything larger than a small area.

30
00:03:27.014 --> 00:03:40.320
Back on the scale. Ngozi's pot weighed 1,800 g empty, so with 5 kg of cream it should read 6,800 g. It read 6,640 g.

31
00:03:40.685 --> 00:03:51.357
She stirred back 160 g of boiled, cooled water. Rest 24 hours, check pH is about 4 to 5.5, then fill wide-neck jars.

32
00:03:52.357 --> 00:04:02.419
Now go through the lessons below. Make your test shampoo and user panel, your 2-in-1 comparison, and your first 1 kg conditioner with a temperature log.

